From 9196ebe9e783fd66227b0e9fdae239a334cb98c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: T3chnobone <98963290+T3chnobone@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:52:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Couch Party / LAN: show every player's HUD, draw karts at any
 distance

- Lap counter, timer and speedometer: the 1P slide-in animation only moved
  player 1's HUD. Every other view kept its starting positions, with the
  lap counter off the left edge and the speedometer off the right. The
  slide-in now runs for every human driver, and the speedometer needle
  sits on each player's own dial.
- Left-side HUD pictures (lap counter) moved only their left edge with the
  screen edge. In a view narrower than 4:3, such as two players side by
  side, the right edge ended up left of the left edge and the picture
  vanished. Both edges now move together.
- Karts: the stock draw distance (tuned for the N64) made karts vanish a
  few hundred units ahead. In Couch Party and LAN races every kart is now
  drawn at any distance.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qq7B1sWVXKm11Pn2wqQeQQ
